        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.047,
            0.563,
            0.218,
            0.576
          ],
          "content": "I can do something = I know how to do it, or it is possible for me to do it."
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "bbox": [
            0.058,
            0.577,
            0.214,
            0.669
          ],
          "sub_type": "text",
          "content": "☐ I can play the piano. My brother can play the piano too.\nSarah can speak Italian, but she can't speak Spanish.\n□ A: Can you swim?\n8: Yes, but I'm not a very good swimmer.\nA: Can you change twenty pounds?\nB: I'm sorry, I can't.\nI'm having a party next week, but Paul and Rachel can't come."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.034,
            0.681,
            0.036,
            0.695
          ],
          "content": "\\-"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.046,
            0.68,
            0.196,
            0.693
          ],
          "content": "For the past (yesterday / last week etc.), we use could/couldn't:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.058,
            0.694,
            0.164,
            0.706
          ],
          "content": "When I was young, I could run very fast."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.058,
            0.706,
            0.266,
            0.732
          ],
          "content": "Before Maria came to Britain, she couldn't understand much English. Now she can understand everything."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.058,
            0.733,
            0.165,
            0.746
          ],
          "content": "☐ I was tired last night, but I couldn't sleep."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.058,
            0.746,
            0.207,
            0.76
          ],
          "content": "☐ I had a party last week, but Paul and Rachel couldn't come."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.034,
            0.772,
            0.036,
            0.785
          ],
          "content": "C"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.046,
            0.77,
            0.17,
            0.784
          ],
          "content": "Can you ... ? Could you ... ? Can I ... ? Could I ... ?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.046,
            0.79,
            0.221,
            0.803
          ],
          "content": "We use Can you ... ? or Could you ... ? when we ask people to do things:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.058,
            0.803,
            0.235,
            0.816
          ],
          "content": "Can you open the door, please? or Could you open the door, please?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.058,
            0.816,
            0.204,
            0.83
          ],
          "content": "Can you wait a moment, please? or Could you wait ... ?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.046,
            0.836,
            0.192,
            0.849
          ],
          "content": "We use Can I have \\_? or Can I get \\_? to ask for something."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.058,
            0.849,
            0.194,
            0.863
          ],
          "content": "Can I have a glass of water, please? or Can I get ... ?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.046,
            0.868,
            0.172,
            0.881
          ],
          "content": "Can I ... ? or Could I ... ? = is it OK to do something?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.058,
            0.881,
            0.101,
            0.893
          ],
          "content": "Can I sit here!"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.058,
            0.893,
            0.154,
            0.907
          ],
          "content": "☐ Tom, could I borrow your umbrella?"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.245,
            0.354,
            0.265
          ],
          "level": 2,
